Fuzix for the 48K ZX Spectrum with a DIVIDE+

The 48K spectrum has provision to page out the ROM in the low 16K via the
expansion bus. The standard DivIDE has a load of magic that prevents this
as it's intended to page in and act as disk drive and firmware for it, but
the DivIDE+ also just lets you map any of the extra RAM pages into the low 16K
which will do just fine.

Memory map:
0000-2FFF:	Banked code: buffers/fonts are also banked
		Buffers must be in overlay4 (bank 3)
3000-3FFF:	Copies of common code space (to leave us room in 5B00-7FFF)
4000-5AFF:	Screen
5B00-7FFF:	Writable kernel space
8000-FFFF:	User live copy

On a task switch we put the old 8000-FFFF into the two user blocks assigned
to that task, we then reverse the process for the two user blocks.

Execution model is thus actually that the other ram banks are "swap". We need
special care with the ramdisk copiers because we'll be swapping the main
commonmem out

In theory we can also load binaries 8000-FFFF and if they'd have less space for
data maybe load data 0000-3FFF. Might need reloc changes though. Likewise we
might be able to use user 0080-3FFF for malloc space outside the normal banks
but that would require some changes to allocate 3 pages per process and
to rework the user copies to handle overlapped I/O

Booting

The image is raw on the disk in the usual PC boot area with partition table
and ESXDOS in the first partition. The bootloader is a simple ESXDOS program
that raw loads the disk blocks. It might be nicer to put the bits on the
ESXDOS file system ?

Boot the machine with the disk image. Type ".fuzix". Enjoy.

